and maintenance and support for license subscriptions; and professional and customer support services. In addition, the company offers platforms, such as artificial intelligence, low-code, data fabric, process automation, intelligent document processing, process mining, process intelligence, and case management studio; and solutions, including federal acquisition, public sector case management, state and local e-procurement, contract lifecycle management, insurance connected underwriting, and insurance claims processing. It serves financial services, government, life sciences, insurance, manufacturing, energy, healthcare, telecommunications, and transportation industries. The company has a collaboration with Deloitte Touche Tohmatsu Limited for the development of AI-Powered Policing solutions. Appian Corporation forms strategic partnership with PSI CRO to advance an AI-driven process orchestration solution that automates clinical trial site identification and selection across therapeutic areas, indications, and geographies. Appian Corporation was incorporated in 1999 and is headquartered in McLean, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew W. Calkins | Founder, Chairman, CEO & President | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $338K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 19%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $28K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $19K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Appian Corporation is a mid-cap technology business with a $3.9B market cap on $727M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +16% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.3pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -110% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 72% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $60M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 50.99\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.5%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 6.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 374% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":3.735776946194129},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $8.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Appian (APPN) Overvalued On Strong Earnings Guidance And Defense Wins?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nasdaq-appn/appian/news/is-appian-appn-overvalued-on-strong-earnings-guidance-and-de","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794459034.85,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.923,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Appian (APPN) vs. Its Rivals Financial Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/appian-appn-vs-its-rivals-financial-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794390304.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.586,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Appian (NASDAQ:APPN) Stock: Insider Matthew Calkins Sells 30,000 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/appian-nasdaqappn-stock-insider-matthew-calkins-sells-30000-shares.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794388135.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.896,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Understanding Momentu